Skilltrees / Edha — License
===========================

This repository mixes two kinds of thing, and they are licensed differently. This split
(and the wording below) is the maintainer's choice, made for a homebrew project — it is
not legal advice.

Unofficial fan content
-----------------------

Edha is unofficial, fan-created content for the Cosmere RPG. This project is not
affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Dragonsteel Entertainment or Brotherwise
Games. Cosmere, Stormlight, and the Cosmere RPG are the intellectual property of their
respective owners. No rules text, art, or other material from the published Cosmere RPG
books is reproduced in this repository; the Cosmere RPG rulebook is required to use this
project's content, and it is not included here or for sale. Nothing in this repository
may be sold.

What counts as "code" vs. "content"
------------------------------------

**Code** — licensed MIT (below): everything under `scripts/`, `module-src/`, `tests/`,
and `.github/`; the build/tooling manifests (`package.json`, `.gitattributes`,
`.gitignore`); and any other script that builds, tests, lints, or automates the project,
including a small helper script that happens to live inside a `.claude/skills/*` folder
(for example `audit.py` or `validate-build.py`).

**Content** — licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (below): everything under `data/`, `docs/`, and
`source-materials/`; the root-level `EDHA_*.md` / `EDHA_*.html` documents and the
project's other prose documents (`README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `AUTHORING_WORKFLOW.md`,
`TODO_REPO_HYGIENE.md`, `TODO_WORLDBUILDING.md`, `TRIAGE_PLAYTEST_PC_MANUALS.md`,
`FORCED_MOVEMENT_PILOT.md`); the prose under `.claude/agents/` and `.claude/skills/`
(skill guides, case studies, session context); and the homebrew game material itself —
talent trees, card text, lore canon, campaign material, and adversary blocks — wherever
in the repository it appears. When it is unclear which side a file falls on, the content
license applies, since the point of this split is to protect the game material.

